<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Pyritz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1493">1493</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrzyce">Pyritz</a>, concluded in 1493 at Pyrzyce, settled the long dispute between the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-x">Bogislaw X</a> and the Margraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> over Brandenburg's claim to overlordship. Brandenburg gave up the claim in return for the right to inherit Pomerania if the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a> died out. When the line ended in 1637, this claim clashed with Swedish occupation of the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pyritz.jpg" alt="Treaty of Pyritz" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Cicero.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
